# Testing Rules (Unit Tests Only)

## Scope Decision
- Java UNIT tests in core/src/test: IN SCOPE
- Integration tests (it.tests module): OUT OF SCOPE — do not use
- E2E tests (ui.tests / Cypress): OUT OF SCOPE — do not write Cypress specs
- The it.tests and ui.tests modules remain generated but UNUSED

## Framework
- JUnit 5 (Jupiter)
- Sling/AEM Mocks (io.wcm.testing.mock.aem / org.apache.sling.testing) only where needed
- Mock repositories when testing services (test business logic in isolation)

## Required Coverage — State Machine (highest priority)
- Location: core/src/test/java/com/mysite/core/statemachine
- Every VALID transition succeeds:
    Open->In Progress, In Progress->Resolved, Resolved->Closed,
    Open->Cancelled, In Progress->Cancelled
- Representative INVALID transitions are rejected (throw InvalidTransitionException):
    Open->Resolved, Open->Closed, In Progress->Closed, Resolved->Open,
    Resolved->In Progress, Closed->*, Cancelled->*

## Service-Layer Unit Tests
- TicketService: create defaults status=Open, validation rejects blank title/invalid enum,
  reassign rejects unknown user, changeStatus delegates to state machine
- CommentService: rejects empty message, rejects comment on non-existent ticket

## Conventions
- Behavior-named tests: shouldAllowOpenToInProgress(), shouldRejectResolvedToOpen()
- Arrange-Act-Assert; no test depends on another test's state
- Run with: mvn test

## Do NOT
- Do NOT scaffold or edit it.tests or ui.tests
- Do NOT add Cypress specs or E2E dependencies
